From: telegdyd <telegdyd93@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] jasmine: system sleep (stock system-pc + RPM sleep set), modem watch on interrupts

Power plan item 4. When the last core goes down, both L2s are down, the display is off and every
core's next timer is at least 15.3 ms away (stock sdm660 lpm-levels "system-pc": entry 10831 us
+ exit 4506 us), cpuidle asks PSCI for the system level (StateID 0x42000343, notify-rpm). As
qcom-mpm.c the vMPM in RPM message RAM (0x7781b8) gets the broadcast timer's compare value as
the wake time and the SPMI arbiter pin 87 (Power key, charger) as a wake pin, then APCS IPC bit 1.
The RPM applies the AP's sleep set: sweet_rpm_sleep_votes() level 1 sets every RPM clock off
there but rf_clk1_pin (Linux after boot, so XO can shut down), level 2 also VDD_CX/MX at
retention (VDD min). The active set never changes. `cpuidle sys N` (0 off, 1 system level,
2 + XO shutdown votes, 3 + rails), boot-arg sweetsys=; `cpuidle sys` shows the census (why the
system level was not taken, which timer was too soon) and the RPM master stats (shutdowns, XO
shutdowns per master).

The modem watch loop's idle step polled every 5 ms, which alone kept the system level away.
Now the GLINK interrupt from the modem (SPI 452, edge) and the copy-complete interrupts of the
host receive CEs (SPI 413-425, HOST_IE bit 0, HOST_IS cleared before the sleep, lines unmasked
only while the loop sleeps) wake it, and with the screen off the step is a 1 s fallback.
modem_irq=0: polling as before. The WCN3990 LDO votes go to both sets (as icnss's regulators),
so the chip keeps power while the AP sleeps.

